### 5. Panic on Invalid Input
**Component**: Parser, Lexer
**Severity**: 🟠 HIGH
**Problem**:
```rust
fn read_number(&mut self) -> Token {
    let mut s = String::new();
    while self.current_char().map_or(false, |c| c.is_numeric()) {
        s.push(self.current_char().unwrap());  // ❌ Could panic
        self.advance();
    }
    Token::Integer(s.parse().unwrap_or(0))  // ❌ unwrap_or hides errors
}
```

**Risk**:
- Unexpected panics
- Unreliable error messages
- Crashes instead of graceful errors

**Fix**:
```rust
fn read_number(&mut self) -> Result<Token, CompileError> {
    let mut s = String::new();
    while let Some(c) = self.current_char() {
        if !c.is_numeric() && c != '.' {
            break;
        }
        s.push(c);
        self.advance();
    }

    if s.is_empty() {
        return Err(CompileError::LexerError("Empty number".to_string()));
    }

    if s.contains('.') {
        s.parse::<f64>()
            .map(Token::Float)
            .map_err(|_| CompileError::LexerError(
                format!("Invalid float: {}", s)
            ))
    } else {
        s.parse::<i64>()
            .map(Token::Integer)
            .map_err(|_| CompileError::LexerError(
                format!("Invalid integer: {}", s)
            ))
    }
}
```

